Give the RTSP keep-alive a body.

GND pings the sink every 25s with an empty GET_PARAMETER (RFC 2326's keep-alive).
An LG webOS panel tears the whole session down in response, reproducibly within
about a second:

  13:03:31.150  WfdClient: Doing keep-alive
                rtsp-client.c:1589 handle_teardown_request: no aggregate path
                  /wfd1.0/streamid=0
  13:03:32.427  NdWFDMiceSink: Client connection removed

OPTIONS "*" is the other conventional RTSP keep-alive and fares worse, ~0.16s.
Not pinging at all is no better: the sink then closes the connection itself after
a fixed ~35s (measured 32s, 35s, 37s across three sessions).

What it does accept is a GET_PARAMETER carrying a body -- that is the M3 exchange
it answers during setup. Asking for one parameter it already returned there keeps
the session open indefinitely: five pings, five 200s, no teardown, where every
bodyless form died in under 35s.

The request URI is not involved; the same "rtsp://localhost/wfd1.0" is used for
the SET_PARAMETER exchanges the sink accepts at M3/M4.

GND_KEEPALIVE=none restores the previous do-not-ping behaviour.

Not upstreamed.

--- a/src/wfd/wfd-client.c
+++ b/src/wfd/wfd-client.c
@@ -379,9 +379,23 @@
       return GST_RTSP_FILTER_REMOVE;
     }

+  /* GND_KEEPALIVE=none restores the old behaviour of not pinging at all. */
+  if (!g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("GND_KEEPALIVE"), "none"))
+    {
+      g_debug ("WfdClient: Skipping keep-alive ping (GND_KEEPALIVE=none)");
+      gst_rtsp_session_touch (sess);
+      return GST_RTSP_FILTER_KEEP;
+    }
+
   g_debug ("WfdClient: Doing keep-alive");

+  /* The body is what matters: an LG webOS panel tears the session down on a
+   * bodyless ping but answers one carrying a parameter, as it does at M3. */
   gst_rtsp_message_init_request (&msg, GST_RTSP_GET_PARAMETER, "rtsp://localhost/wfd1.0");
+  gst_rtsp_message_add_header_by_name (&msg, "Content-Type", "text/parameters");
+  gst_rtsp_message_set_body (&msg,
+                             (const guint8 *) "wfd_audio_codecs\r\n",
+                             strlen ("wfd_audio_codecs\r\n"));

   res = gst_rtsp_client_send_message (client, sess, &msg);
   if (res != GST_RTSP_OK)
